  "rationale": "The requirement asks for one structural item: a public async method `search_structure` on `impl Sources`. It takes `&self` and `query: &StructuralQuery`, and returns `Result<StructuralMatches, SourceError>`. `crates/trust-but-verify/src/sources/public.rs#impl[Sources]/fn[search_structure]` has exactly that signature and is marked `{impl}`. It delegates to `self.analysis.search_structure(query).await`. The `analysis` field of `struct[Sources]` is `SourceAnalysis<LocalSources>`. `LocalSources` implements `SourceProvider` with `type Error = SourceError`. So the delegate `crates/trust-but-verify/src/sources.rs#impl[SourceAnalysis<P>]/fn[search_structure]`, which returns `Result<StructuralMatches, P::Error>`, gives `Result<StructuralMatches, SourceError>` here. The delegate is also marked `{impl}` and calls the provider's `search_structure`. `StructuralMatches` is the public alias `SearchResults<StructuralMatch>` in `sources/public.rs`. I found no structural gap. I did not assess the independent behavioral check.",
